  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about plumbers in Anna</h2>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best plumber in Anna, TX?</h3><p>For 2026, our top pick is Hometown Plumbing, based on Magnolia St in Anna. It's the only one of the four companies we checked with a quantified independent review count (111 on Birdeye) and it advertises 24-hour availability. Umbrella Plumbing Company (BBB A+ rating) and Evans Professional Plumbing (corroborated across three independent directories) are also strong, Anna-headquartered options.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Why does Anna have so many slab leak repairs?</h3><p>Like most of North Texas, Anna is built on slab-on-grade foundations over expansive clay soil that swells and shrinks with moisture. That movement stresses the water lines running under the slab, particularly in newer subdivisions still settling — so slab leak detection and repair is a routine, well-established service category here, not a rare specialty call.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How much do common plumbing repairs cost in Anna?</h3><p>Drain clearing, toilet repairs and faucet fixes typically run $125–$450 across North Texas, with a $50–$95 service call fee and $75–$150 hourly rates. Slab leak repairs run far wider, from roughly $1,500 for an accessible spot repair to $15,000 for extensive tunneling.</p></div>
